 Yaw Estimation Limitation

The current system uses a 6DOF IMU (accelerometer + gyroscope).

While roll and pitch can be stabilized using gravity as a reference, yaw estimation relies solely on gyroscope integration.

Since no magnetometer or external heading reference is available, yaw is subject to drift and cannot be absolutely corrected.

Future improvements:

Add magnetometer (9DOF)

Implement sensor fusion with heading reference

Explore extended Kalman filtering
